# Codex layer: what differs from the tool-neutral subagents/<name>.md for Codex.
# One line per setting: <agent> <key> <value>. Each becomes `key = "value"` in
# ~/.codex/agents/<agent>.toml. Anthropic model names mean nothing to Codex, so
# no agent sets `model` and Codex uses its own default; add `<agent> model <id>`
# to pin one. Codex has no per-agent tool list, only a sandbox.
#
# `<agent> skip` keeps an agent out of Codex entirely: nothing is generated, and
# a file this script generated earlier is removed. Uncomment to turn one off.
#
# Existing files in ~/.codex/agents that this script did not generate are never
# touched, so an agent with its own Codex file already is left as it is.
# powershell-expert skip
# finance-analyst skip
# andrew-voice-writer skip

accessibility-tester sandbox_mode read-only
architect-reviewer sandbox_mode read-only
code-reviewer sandbox_mode read-only
research-analyst sandbox_mode read-only
security-auditor sandbox_mode read-only
